profile.TRES_LEGER=Very light
profile.LEGER=Light
profile.EQUILIBRE=Balanced
profile.BEAU=Beautiful
screen.MIST=Mist
screen.LIGHT=Light and shadows
screen.NATURE=Wind
screen.COLOR=Colours
option.MIST_DENSITY=Mist density
option.MIST_DENSITY.comment=How thick the mist is at ground level.
option.MIST_HEIGHT=Mist height
option.MIST_HEIGHT.comment=Height, in blocks, over which the mist thins out above the ground.
option.MIST_LIFT=Lift inside a clearing
option.MIST_LIFT.comment=Share of the surrounding mist that lifts while you stand in a clearing.
option.MIST_RING=Distant ring
option.MIST_RING.comment=Strength of the ring of mist that always closes the horizon.
option.MIST_RING_MAX=Ring distance
option.MIST_RING_MAX.comment=Farthest distance of the ring, in blocks, when Distant Horizons draws the far landscape.
option.AIR_DENSITY=Distant air
option.AIR_DENSITY.comment=Far terrain takes the colour of the sky, blue first; thicker in a humid biome.
option.FOG_STEPS=Volumetric mist
option.FOG_STEPS.comment=Steps of the march through the near mist: it rolls into banks, the sun cuts rays into it and torches glow in it. Off: the mist is a smooth layer.
value.FOG_STEPS.0=Off
option.FOG_RANGE=Volumetric mist reach
option.FOG_RANGE.comment=How far the marched mist reaches; beyond it, the mist is a smooth layer.
option.FOG_BILLOWS=Mist banks
option.FOG_BILLOWS.comment=How much the mist rolls into denser banks and thinner gaps, drifting with the wind.
option.FOG_BLOCK_GLOW=Glow of lights in mist
option.FOG_BLOCK_GLOW.comment=Torches, lanterns and lava light the mist around them in their colour.
option.CAVE_HAZE=Cave haze
option.CAVE_HAZE.comment=A faint dust underground that only lights make visible.
option.CAVE_DETAIL=Caves and lava
option.CAVE_DETAIL.comment=Molten lava with drifting crust, hot air trembling above it and damp rock that catches the light of torches.
value.CAVE_DETAIL.0=Off
value.CAVE_DETAIL.1=On
option.CAVE_DRIPS=Cave drips
option.CAVE_DRIPS.comment=Under cave ceilings, water falls drop by drop, always in the same places, and gleams in torchlight.
value.CAVE_DRIPS.0=Off
value.CAVE_DRIPS.1=On
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow resolution
option.shadowDistance=Shadow distance
option.SHADOW_FILTER=Shadow softness
option.SHADOW_FILTER.comment=Samples per pixel. More is smoother and slower.
option.sunPathRotation=Sun path tilt
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS=Light shafts
option.LIGHT_SHAFTS.comment=Steps used to draw sunbeams in the mist. 0 turns them off.
option.SHAFT_STRENGTH=Shaft strength
option.MOON_SHAFTS=Moonbeams
option.MOON_SHAFTS.comment=At night, beams of moonlight show in the mist where trees and walls cut them, as the eye used to the dark sees them, much brighter than the light the moon casts on the ground. Needs light shafts. Strong makes them brighter still.
value.MOON_SHAFTS.0=Off
value.MOON_SHAFTS.1=On
value.MOON_SHAFTS.2=Strong
option.BLOOM=Glow
option.BLOOM.comment=Soft halo around the brightest lights.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Glow strength
option.WIND_STRENGTH=Wind on plants
option.FOLIAGE_SHEEN=Grass sheen
option.FOLIAGE_SHEEN.comment=Grass and flowers bent by the wind or by steps show their paler underside: gusts cross a meadow in light waves.
option.PLANT_ROOTS=Shaded plant feet
option.PLANT_ROOTS.comment=The lower part of grass, flowers and crops darkens, as in a tuft where the blades shade each other: meadows gain depth.
option.PLANT_ROOTS_DEPTH=Plant feet depth
option.PLANT_ROOTS_DEPTH.comment=How dark the foot of plants gets.
option.LEAF_FLUTTER=Fluttering leaves
option.LEAF_FLUTTER.comment=In the wind, leaves turn and catch the sun for an instant: a few texels of the foliage light up and go out, more often in strong wind.
option.WATER_PLANT_SWAY=Swaying water plants
option.WATER_PLANT_SWAY.comment=Seagrass and kelp sway slowly in the current, the whole stem in one piece, and lily pads lift and tilt on the ripples.
option.LANTERN_SWAY=Swinging lanterns
option.LANTERN_SWAY.comment=Hanging lanterns swing in the wind around their hook, more in a storm; under a roof they stay still.
option.GRASS_TUFTS=Fuller tufts
option.GRASS_TUFTS.comment=Each nearby grass, flower and crop gets a turned copy, short grass a little taller or shorter: meadows lose their grid of crosses and look fuller. Same distance as bushy leaves.
option.BUSHY_DISTANCE=Grass tufts range
option.BUSHY_DISTANCE.comment=How far, in blocks, grass tufts are fuller.
option.WATER_WAVES=Water waves
screen.WATER=Water
option.WATER_MURK=Water murk
option.WATER_MURK.comment=Higher: the bottom fades sooner and the water takes its colour.
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS=Landscape reflections
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Steps searching the banks and trees mirrored in the water; 0: the sky only.
option.VOXEL_REFLECTIONS=Off-screen reflections
option.VOXEL_REFLECTIONS.comment=Blocks walked to find what the screen does not show (the bank behind you, a tree out of frame) in water, ice and puddles; 0: only what is on screen.
option.REFLECT_LEAF_GAPS=Leaf gaps in reflections
option.REFLECT_LEAF_GAPS.comment=In off-screen reflections, foliage lets the sky through in places, a quarter block at a time: a tree reflected in a pond reads as a dappled crown, not a solid mass.
value.REFLECT_LEAF_GAPS.0=Off
value.REFLECT_LEAF_GAPS.1=On
option.WATER_CAUSTICS=Caustics
option.WATER_CAUSTICS.comment=The threads of light the waves draw on the bottom.
value.WATER_CAUSTICS.0=Off
value.WATER_CAUSTICS.1=Soft
value.WATER_CAUSTICS.2=Strong
option.WATER_PIXELS=Pixel waves
option.WATER_PIXELS.comment=The waves follow the grid of the textures, with hard-edged reflections.
value.WATER_PIXELS.0=Off
value.WATER_PIXELS.1=On
option.WATER_MOTES=Marine snow
option.WATER_MOTES.comment=Under water, suspended specks that drift and catch the light, most of all against the sun.
option.WATER_WAKES=Wakes
option.WATER_WAKES.comment=What crosses the water ripples it: a boat leaves a V-shaped wake and foam, a swimmer rings. Needs the fallow mod.
option.WATER_FOAM=Surf
option.WATER_FOAM.comment=Surf along the banks: a fringe that breathes, and bands of foam rolling in from open water.
value.WATER_MOTES.0=Off
value.WATER_MOTES.1=On
option.AIR_MOTES=Dust in the light
option.AIR_MOTES.comment=Specks floating where the sun gets through, under the trees or by a window, brightest against the light.
value.AIR_MOTES.0=Off
value.AIR_MOTES.1=On
option.OLIVE=Olive greens
option.OLIVE.comment=Pulls the greens of grass and leaves toward a warm olive green, that of a dry summer, instead of the bluish greens of the game.
option.FOLIAGE_TONE=Summer foliage
option.FOLIAGE_TONE.comment=Gives grass and leaves back the warm yellow-green of a summer day, which the air and the haze had dulled to grey-green. Sky, clouds, mist, stone and water are left alone.
option.GROUND_TINT=Landscape shades
option.GROUND_TINT.comment=Across wide patches, grass and leaves lean toward a drier yellowed green here and a deeper lush green there, and bare ground is a little lighter or darker: the repeated textures show less from afar.
value.GROUND_TINT.0=Off
value.GROUND_TINT.1=On
option.GRASS_OVERHANG=Grass overhang
option.GRASS_OVERHANG.comment=On the sides of grass blocks, the green edge hangs a few pixels lower, with a ragged length from one pixel column to the next, instead of stopping on an almost straight line.
value.GRASS_OVERHANG.0=Off
value.GRASS_OVERHANG.1=On
option.GRASS_SLOPES=Grassy slopes
option.GRASS_SLOPES.comment=The step between two grass terraces is covered with grass over its whole height, so a hillside reads as one green slope instead of stripes of dirt. Needs Grass overhang and Off-screen reflections; within about sixty blocks.
option.GRASS_FAR_SIDES=Green far hillsides
option.GRASS_FAR_SIDES.comment=Beyond about fifty blocks, the sides of grass blocks under the sky are covered with grass, like the Distant Horizons hills: no brown ring between the near and the far landscape.
option.FAR_CANOPY=Shaded far forests
option.FAR_CANOPY.comment=Each Distant Horizons leaf block takes its own shade, a little lighter or darker, warmer or cooler, and the underside of crowns darkens: far forests show their trees instead of a flat green paste.
value.GRASS_SLOPES.0=Off
value.GRASS_SLOPES.1=On
option.COLORED_LIGHT=Coloured light
option.COLORED_LIGHT.comment=Torches light in orange, soul lanterns in blue, lava in red, sea lanterns in bluish white; what you hold lights in its colour. Costs a little every frame.
option.GLASS_TINT=Stained glass light
option.GLASS_TINT.comment=Sunlight and moonlight passing through stained glass take its colour, on what they light and in their shafts; dark glass holds the light back. Almost free.
option.SATURATION=Saturation
option.CONTRAST=Contrast
option.EXPOSURE=Exposure
option.EXPOSURE_AUTO=Eye adaptation
option.EXPOSURE_AUTO.comment=The eye gets used to what it looks at: a dark scene opens up, a dazzling one closes, halfway only and over a few seconds (faster toward light than toward darkness).
option.EXPOSURE_AUTO_AMOUNT=Adaptation strength
option.EXPOSURE_AUTO_AMOUNT.comment=How far the eye adapts to the brightness of the scene.
option.EXPOSURE_SPEED=Adaptation speed
option.EXPOSURE_SPEED.comment=How fast the eye adapts.
option.RAIN_GLOOM=Grey rainy days
option.RAIN_GLOOM.comment=Under rain, outdoors, the eye does not open back up fully: a grey day stays dim, in the warm grey of heavy clouds, as in Recrafted (sky around 160 out of 255, ground around 50). Half as strong at night. Off keeps the old exposure; Strong is darker still.
value.RAIN_GLOOM.0=Off
value.RAIN_GLOOM.1=On
value.RAIN_GLOOM.2=Strong
option.DOF=Depth of field
option.DOF.comment=What is far from the point you look at blurs like through a lens; the focus follows the centre of the screen. Soft: a light blur of the distance when looking close. Photo: a marked blur.
value.DOF.0=Off
value.DOF.1=Soft
value.DOF.2=Photo
option.PURKINJE=Night vision
option.PURKINJE.comment=In the dark, colours fade and the image turns slightly blue, as the eye sees at night.
option.NIGHT_GRAIN=Night grain
option.NIGHT_GRAIN.comment=In the dark the eye no longer sees sharply: a fine, colourless grain flickers over the shadows, none over what is lit.
value.NIGHT_GRAIN.0=Off
value.NIGHT_GRAIN.1=On
option.VIGNETTE=Vignette
option.VIGNETTE.comment=The corners of the image darken slightly, as through a lens.
option.AO_SAMPLES=Screen occlusion
option.AO_SAMPLES.comment=Darkens the sky light in hollows, under foliage and at the foot of walls. 0: off.
option.AO_RADIUS=Occlusion reach
option.AO_RADIUS.comment=Size of the hollows taken into account, in blocks.
option.AO_STRENGTH=Occlusion strength
option.AO_STRENGTH.comment=Stronger: darker hollows.
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Soft shadows
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=The edge of a shadow widens with the distance of what casts it, as under a tall tree. 0: sharp edges.
option.SHADOW_SEARCH=Shadow search
option.SHADOW_SEARCH.comment=Samples spent finding how far the shadow caster is, which sets how soft the shadow edge grows.
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS=Contact shadows
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS.comment=A short trace toward the sun on screen finds what the shadow map is too coarse for: grass, ledges, small objects.
value.CONTACT_SHADOWS.0=Off
value.CONTACT_SHADOWS.1=On
option.SSGI=Light bounce
option.SSGI.comment=Rays per pixel gathering the light nearby surfaces send back: a sunlit wall brightens the ground at its foot, lava reddens the rock around it.
value.SSGI.0=Off
option.SSGI_STRENGTH=Bounce strength
option.SSGI_STRENGTH.comment=How much of the gathered bounce light is added.
option.LEAF_TRANSLUCENCY=Leaf translucency
option.LEAF_TRANSLUCENCY.comment=How much sunlight passes through foliage, less through thicker canopy, and glows green against the light.
option.CANOPY_SHADE=Canopy shade
option.CANOPY_SHADE.comment=Under a forest, the ground, trunks and the inside of the foliage get less light from the sky, as each layer of leaves above holds some back, down to a third under a thick canopy. The game only takes away one step of sky light per leaf block, which leaves the undergrowth as bright as an open field. Needs coloured light, shader rain or voxel reflections; best with temporal anti-aliasing. Strong darkens further.
value.CANOPY_SHADE.0=Off
value.CANOPY_SHADE.1=On
value.CANOPY_SHADE.2=Strong
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_SHAPE=Shaped block light
option.BLOCK_LIGHT_SHAPE.comment=Faces turned toward a torch receive more of its light than those turned away, and flames waver softly.
value.BLOCK_LIGHT_SHAPE.0=Off
value.BLOCK_LIGHT_SHAPE.1=On
screen.CLOUDS=Clouds
option.CLOUD_STEPS=Volumetric clouds
option.CLOUD_STEPS.comment=Precision of the clouds (steps). 0: the game's clouds.
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Coverage
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=Share of the sky covered in fair weather; rain adds more.
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT=Height
option.CLOUD_HEIGHT.comment=Height of the cloud base, in blocks.
option.CLOUD_SPEED=Speed
option.CLOUD_SPEED.comment=How fast the wind pushes the clouds.
option.CLOUD_LIGHT=Brightness
option.CLOUD_LIGHT.comment=Sunlight sent back by the clouds.
option.CLOUD_RANGE=Range
option.CLOUD_RANGE.comment=How far the clouds are drawn, in blocks.
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud shadows
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS.comment=Passing clouds darken the ground.
option.CLOUD_TYPES=Cloud kinds
option.CLOUD_TYPES.comment=A slow weather map mixes flat stratocumulus banks, round cumulus and, under thunder, towers that spread into anvils.
value.CLOUD_TYPES.0=One kind
value.CLOUD_TYPES.1=Weather map
option.CLOUD_ALTO=Altocumulus
option.CLOUD_ALTO.comment=A thin layer of small rounded clouds above the main layer, the dappled sky that comes before a change of weather.
option.RAIN_ROLLS=Rain cloud rolls
option.RAIN_ROLLS.comment=Under rain, the grey cloud layer is not even: long darker rolls lie across the wind, with thinner bands between them where a little daylight comes through. Strong opens the bands wider.
value.RAIN_ROLLS.0=Off
value.RAIN_ROLLS.1=On
value.RAIN_ROLLS.2=Strong
value.CLOUD_ALTO.0=Off
value.CLOUD_ALTO.1=Rare
value.CLOUD_ALTO.2=Normal
value.CLOUD_ALTO.3=Frequent
option.CLOUD_IRIDESCENCE=Cloud iridescence
option.CLOUD_IRIDESCENCE.comment=Near the sun or moon, thin cloud edges and the dappled sheet take patches of pastel pink, green and blue.
value.CLOUD_IRIDESCENCE.0=Off
value.CLOUD_IRIDESCENCE.1=On
option.CLOUD_CIRRUS=Cirrus
option.CLOUD_CIRRUS.comment=A high veil of wind-combed ice streaks, far above the cloud layer.
value.CLOUD_CIRRUS.0=Off
value.CLOUD_CIRRUS.1=Sparse
value.CLOUD_CIRRUS.2=Normal
value.CLOUD_CIRRUS.3=Plenty
option.CLOUD_MULTISCATTER=Light inside clouds
option.CLOUD_MULTISCATTER.comment=Orders of multiple scattering: more lets light glow through the heart of a cumulus instead of leaving it dark.
option.CLOUD_LIGHT_STEPS=Cloud self-shadow
option.CLOUD_LIGHT_STEPS.comment=Steps of the cone marched towards the sun or moon from each cloud sample.
option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING=Lightning in clouds
option.CLOUD_LIGHTNING.comment=Strikes light the towers from within, and storms flicker with sheet lightning.
value.CLOUD_LIGHTNING.0=Off
value.CLOUD_LIGHTNING.1=On
option.SKY_METEORS=Shooting stars
option.SKY_METEORS.comment=Now and then a shooting star crosses the clear night sky.
value.SKY_METEORS.0=Off
value.SKY_METEORS.1=On
option.SKY_AURORA=Northern lights
option.SKY_AURORA.comment=On some clear nights in cold lands, green and violet curtains ripple in the sky.
value.SKY_AURORA.0=Off
value.SKY_AURORA.1=On
option.SKY_AURORA_STRENGTH=Northern lights strength
option.SKY_AURORA_STRENGTH.comment=How bright the curtains glow.
option.SKY_STARS=Stars
option.SKY_STARS.comment=Stars of every size and colour that turn with the sky and twinkle more near the horizon.
value.SKY_STARS.0=Vanilla
value.SKY_STARS.1=Starry sky
option.SKY_MILKY_WAY=Milky Way
option.SKY_MILKY_WAY.comment=A band of glow and dust lanes across the night sky, paler under a full moon.
value.SKY_MILKY_WAY.0=Off
value.SKY_MILKY_WAY.1=On
option.SKY_HALO=Ice halos
option.SKY_HALO.comment=The 22° and 46° halos and sun dogs where cirrus crosses the sun or moon.
value.SKY_HALO.0=Off
value.SKY_HALO.1=On
option.SKY_RAINBOW=Rainbow
option.SKY_RAINBOW.comment=When the sun comes back on retreating rain: primary and secondary bows with the dark band between them.
value.SKY_RAINBOW.0=Off
value.SKY_RAINBOW.1=On
screen.RAIN=Rain, snow, heat
option.SHADER_RAIN=Shader rain
option.SHADER_RAIN.comment=Drops and flakes drawn by the shader: pixel-sized, slanted by the wind, stopped by roofs and trees, with passing showers. Off: the game's rain.
option.TRACKS=Footprints
option.TRACKS.comment=Players and animals leave footprints in sand and snow, which fade away.
option.TRACK_MINUTES=Footprint lifetime
option.TRACK_MINUTES.comment=Minutes before a footprint fades; falling snow and rain fill them faster.
option.WETNESS=Wet ground
option.WETNESS.comment=Under rain the ground darkens and shines, then dries within a few minutes; 0: never wet.
option.PUDDLES=Puddles
option.PUDDLES.comment=Puddles in flat hollows, mirroring the landscape and rippled by the drops.
value.PUDDLES.0=Off
value.PUDDLES.1=On
option.PUDDLE_AMOUNT=Puddle extent
option.PUDDLE_ICE=Frozen puddles
option.PUDDLE_ICE.comment=On cold nights after rain, puddles freeze into dull, cracked ice edged with frost, until mid-morning.
value.PUDDLE_ICE.0=Off
value.PUDDLE_ICE.1=On
option.WET_REFLECTIONS=Puddle reflections
option.WET_REFLECTIONS.comment=Steps searching the landscape mirrored in puddles; 0: the sky only.
option.RAIN_CURTAINS=Rain curtains
option.RAIN_CURTAINS.comment=Thin rain streaks over the distance, beyond the drops the game draws.
option.PATCHY_DRYING=Patchy drying
option.PATCHY_DRYING.comment=Wet ground follows the grain of its texture: hollows soak darker, bumps shine, and after the rain it dries in patches, the hollows and the foot of walls last.
option.WALL_RIVULETS=Rivulets on walls
option.WALL_RIVULETS.comment=Under rain, water runs down walls in dark pixel lines, and a bright drop slides down them now and then.
option.WINDOW_RAIN=Rain on windows
option.WINDOW_RAIN.comment=In the rain, drops bead on windows open to the sky and others run down them, leaving a trail.
value.WINDOW_RAIN.0=Off
value.WINDOW_RAIN.1=On
option.WINDOW_FROST=Frost on windows
option.WINDOW_FROST.comment=In bitter cold, frost grows on windows from the frame in white ferns, further at night and in the morning.
value.WINDOW_FROST.0=Off
value.WINDOW_FROST.1=On
option.WET_ENTITIES=Wet creatures
option.WET_ENTITIES.comment=Out in the rain, animals, armour and the player's arm darken and shine; coming out of water, the player streams, then everything dries within half a minute.
value.WET_ENTITIES.0=Off
value.WET_ENTITIES.1=On
option.SNOWY_ENTITIES=Snowy creatures
option.SNOWY_ENTITIES.comment=In falling snow, flakes settle on the backs of animals, on shoulders and helmets, more and more of them.
value.SNOWY_ENTITIES.0=Off
value.SNOWY_ENTITIES.1=On
option.RAIN_SPLASHES=Rain splashes
option.RAIN_SPLASHES.comment=Drops burst on wet ground: a bright pixel, then a small crown that fades.
option.PRECIP_GLOW=Drops lit by lights
option.PRECIP_GLOW.comment=Rain drops and snowflakes near a torch or a lantern catch its colour; drops sparkle toward the sun or the moon.
option.SNOW_BLIZZARD=Blizzard
option.SNOW_BLIZZARD.comment=Under a thunderstorm in a snowy biome, the wind lays the flakes down, faster and denser.
option.GROUND_DRIFT=Blowing snow and sand
option.GROUND_DRIFT.comment=In strong wind, over snowy land or in the desert, pale streaks race along the ground with the wind.
value.GROUND_DRIFT.0=Off
value.GROUND_DRIFT.1=On
option.WATER_STEAM=Steaming water
option.WATER_STEAM.comment=On cool mornings, and at any hour in bitter cold, wisps of mist rise slowly over lakes and rivers.
value.WATER_STEAM.0=Off
value.WATER_STEAM.1=On
option.SNOW_COVER=Snow on trees
option.SNOW_COVER.comment=In a cold biome, snow covers the top of leaves and ledges that see the sky, near and in the distant landscape.
value.SNOW_COVER.0=Off
value.SNOW_COVER.1=On
option.ALPENGLOW=Alpenglow
option.ALPENGLOW.comment=Just after sunset and before sunrise, high snowy peaks keep a pink glow while the valleys are already in shade.
value.ALPENGLOW.0=Off
value.ALPENGLOW.1=On
option.AURORA_GLOW=Aurora light
option.AURORA_GLOW.comment=On aurora nights, open ground and above all snow take a faint green light that ripples slowly as the curtains pass overhead.
value.AURORA_GLOW.0=Off
value.AURORA_GLOW.1=On
option.SNOW_DETAIL=Snow detail
option.SNOW_DETAIL.comment=Laid snow in patches under trees and around lights, with drifts, wind ripples and glints that move with the eye.
value.SNOW_DETAIL.0=Off
value.SNOW_DETAIL.1=On
option.SNOW_BUILDUP=Snow that builds up
option.SNOW_BUILDUP.comment=While snow falls, it creeps under trees, thickens on the needles and sticks to trunks, walls and rocks facing the wind; it stays while it is cold.
value.SNOW_BUILDUP.0=Off
value.SNOW_BUILDUP.1=On
option.SNOW_SLOPES=Snowy slopes
option.SNOW_SLOPES.comment=In snow, the step between two terraces of a hillside turns white over almost its whole height, its foot ragged to the pixel: the slope reads white in one piece instead of stripes of dirt. Within about sixty blocks.
value.SNOW_SLOPES.0=Off
value.SNOW_SLOPES.1=On
option.SAND_DETAIL=Wind-rippled sand
option.SAND_DETAIL.comment=Sand takes small ripples across the wind, gentle on the windward side and steep behind, whose crests catch the sun.
value.SAND_DETAIL.0=Off
value.SAND_DETAIL.1=On
option.ICE_DETAIL=Cracked ice
option.ICE_DETAIL.comment=Ice shows white cracks that follow large cells, a few fine fractures and bubbles caught inside.
value.ICE_DETAIL.0=Off
value.ICE_DETAIL.1=On
option.CANOPY_DRIPS=Drips and snow from branches
option.CANOPY_DRIPS.comment=Under trees, during and after rain, water drips from the leaves; loaded with snow, branches drop clumps of it when the wind blows.
value.CANOPY_DRIPS.0=Off
value.CANOPY_DRIPS.1=On
option.MATERIALS=Block materials
option.MATERIALS.comment=Each block has its own surface: polished stone, glazed terracotta and gems catch the sun in a sharp glint, metals reflect in their own colour, copper dulls as it oxidises, the mineral of ores shines while the stone around stays matte, wool has a soft sheen at a grazing angle and sculk veins glow faintly. Wet ground turns smooth and the sun draws a bright streak on it.
value.MATERIALS.0=Off
value.MATERIALS.1=On
option.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS=Reflections by roughness
option.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS.comment=Polished stone, gems, metal and wet ground reflect the scene and nearby blocks, sharp on smooth surfaces and blurred on rougher ones; under a roof they no longer reflect the sky.
value.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS.0=Off
value.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS.1=On
option.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS_STRENGTH=Strength of block reflections
option.ROUGH_REFLECTIONS_STRENGTH.comment=How much polished blocks and metals reflect.
option.LABPBR=Resource pack PBR maps
option.LABPBR.comment=With a resource pack in the labPBR format, its normal, height, occlusion, material and emission maps replace the relief drawn from the textures and the block material table.
value.LABPBR.0=Off
value.LABPBR.1=On
option.SPECULAR_STRENGTH=Sun glints
option.SPECULAR_STRENGTH.comment=Strength of the sun's reflection on block surfaces.
option.ORE_GLINTS=Ore glints
option.ORE_GLINTS.comment=In ores, gem blocks and amethyst, some texels catch the light of a nearby torch, of the one you hold or of the sun in a bright point; moving your head lights up others. Needs Materials.
value.ORE_GLINTS.0=Off
value.ORE_GLINTS.1=On
value.ORE_GLINTS.2=Strong
option.FROST=Frost
option.FROST.comment=On cool nights, grass and leaves that see the sky whiten pixel by pixel; the frost melts by mid-morning.
option.RELIEF=Block relief
option.RELIEF.comment=Gives the blocks a pixel relief drawn from their textures: darker texels are hollows, lighter ones bumps. Low light models stone, bark and planks.
option.RELIEF_STRENGTH=Relief strength
option.RELIEF_STRENGTH.comment=How much the light follows the slope of each texel.
option.RELIEF_DEPTH=Relief depth
option.RELIEF_DEPTH.comment=Depth of the relief, in blocks: the eye slides over it and bumps hide the hollows behind them.
option.RELIEF_STEPS=Relief steps
option.RELIEF_STEPS.comment=Steps of the march through the relief (parallax). Off: the relief only shades, it does not move.
value.RELIEF_STEPS.0=Off
option.RELIEF_SHADOWS=Relief shadows
option.RELIEF_SHADOWS.comment=A hollow turned away from the sun stays in the shadow of the bump beside it.
option.RELIEF_BEVEL=Block edges
option.RELIEF_BEVEL.comment=The edge texel of each face leans outward and catches the light: the edges of blocks show.
option.RELIEF_RANGE=Relief range
option.RELIEF_RANGE.comment=Up to what distance the relief is drawn, in blocks.
value.FROST.0=Off
value.FROST.1=On
option.DEW=Dew
option.DEW.comment=On mild mornings in warm, damp biomes, grass and plants are covered in dew that sparkles in the low sun until mid-morning.
value.DEW.0=Off
value.DEW.1=On
option.WET_FOLIAGE=Wet foliage
option.WET_FOLIAGE.comment=After a shower, leaves and grass keep their drops: foliage darkens a little and sparkles when the sun returns.
value.WET_FOLIAGE.0=Off
value.WET_FOLIAGE.1=On
option.HEAT_SHIMMER=Heat shimmer
option.HEAT_SHIMMER.comment=In a desert, in the sun, the distance shimmers near the ground.
value.HEAT_SHIMMER.0=Off
value.HEAT_SHIMMER.1=On
option.FLAME_SHIMMER=Heat above fires
option.FLAME_SHIMMER.comment=Above a fire, a campfire or a lantern, the hot air makes what you see through it ripple.
value.FLAME_SHIMMER.0=Off
value.FLAME_SHIMMER.1=On
option.SMAA=Anti-aliasing
option.SMAA.comment=Smooths the stair-stepped edges of blocks and objects (SMAA). Off: no smoothing, the fastest.
value.SMAA.0=Off
value.SMAA.1=Medium
value.SMAA.2=High
value.SMAA.3=Ultra
option.TAA=Temporal anti-aliasing
option.TAA.comment=Blends each frame with the previous ones: foliage, fences and distant edges stop shimmering as you move. Cheap.
option.TAA_SHARPEN=Sharpening
option.TAA_SHARPEN.comment=Gives back the grain of textures softened by temporal anti-aliasing; stronger in soft areas, held back on edges.
option.TAA_DISOCCLUSION=Disocclusion
option.TAA_DISOCCLUSION.comment=What appears from behind a moving object drops the history of that object at once: no ghost trail around the hand, mobs or trunks when turning.
value.TAA.0=Off
value.TAA.1=On
option.MOTION_BLUR=Motion blur
option.MOTION_BLUR.comment=When the camera turns or moves fast, the image streaks along the motion, like a film camera. Nothing changes when standing still; the hand stays sharp. Cheap.
value.MOTION_BLUR.0=Off
value.MOTION_BLUR.1=Light
value.MOTION_BLUR.2=Medium
value.MOTION_BLUR.3=Strong
value.MOTION_BLUR.4=Very strong
option.FAR_SHADOWS=Distant shadows
option.FAR_SHADOWS.comment=Beyond the shadow map, hills, mountains and forests still cast their shadow on the far landscape, Distant Horizons included. More steps reach further and miss fewer thin ridges.
value.FAR_SHADOWS.0=Off
value.FAR_SHADOWS.16=16 steps
value.FAR_SHADOWS.24=24 steps
value.FAR_SHADOWS.32=32 steps
option.WATER_WAVE_COUNT=Wave trains
option.WATER_WAVE_COUNT.comment=How many wave trains make the surface: swell, wind waves and ripples. More: a richer, less regular sea.
option.WATER_SWELL=Swell
option.WATER_SWELL.comment=The long waves that rise on open water; small ponds stay calm whatever this says.
option.WATER_CHOP=Crest sharpness
option.WATER_CHOP.comment=How much the crests gather and sharpen (Gerstner waves); at strong wind they break into whitecaps.
option.WATER_REFRACTION=Refraction steps
option.WATER_REFRACTION.comment=Steps following the bent ray down to the bottom; 0: a cheap offset instead.
option.WATER_BLUR=Rough reflections
option.WATER_BLUR.comment=Ripples too small to see blur the reflection, more with distance and rain. Needs anti-aliasing.
value.WATER_BLUR.0=Off
value.WATER_BLUR.1=On
option.WATER_DISPERSION=Iridescent caustics
option.WATER_DISPERSION.comment=Red and blue bend slightly differently: the edges of the light threads on the bottom catch a rainbow.
value.WATER_DISPERSION.0=Off
value.WATER_DISPERSION.1=On
option.WATER_FLOW=Current
option.WATER_FLOW.comment=Flowing water carries its ripples down the slope, and foams where it runs fastest.
value.WATER_FLOW.0=Off
value.WATER_FLOW.1=On
option.WATER_WHITECAPS=Whitecaps
option.WATER_WHITECAPS.comment=In strong wind and storms on open water, the crests that fold over break into foam that trails behind them.
value.WATER_WHITECAPS.0=Off
value.WATER_WHITECAPS.1=On
option.WATER_FALLS=Waterfalls
option.WATER_FALLS.comment=Streaks running down falling water, and a churning, foaming ring where it lands.
value.WATER_FALLS.0=Off
value.WATER_FALLS.1=On
option.SHORE_WET=Wet shores
option.SHORE_WET.comment=Sand, earth and stone touching water are dark and shiny up to a block or so from the edge, along a waterline that slowly rises and falls.
value.SHORE_WET.0=Off
value.SHORE_WET.1=On
option.SUN_GLARE=Sun glare
option.SUN_GLARE.comment=Looking toward the sun: a veil around it, which goes out when a cloud or a tree hides it. Camera adds fine rays and a few pale lens reflections.
value.SUN_GLARE.0=Off
value.SUN_GLARE.1=Eye
value.SUN_GLARE.2=Camera
option.SUN_GLARE_STRENGTH=Sun glare strength
option.SUN_GLARE_STRENGTH.comment=How strong the rays and lens reflections are.
option.LENS_DIRT=Lens dirt
option.LENS_DIRT.comment=Facing the sun or a bright light, dust on the lens lights up in soft spots.
value.LENS_DIRT.0=Off
value.LENS_DIRT.1=On
option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION=Chromatic aberration
option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION.comment=The colours part slightly toward the edges of the image, as through a lens.
value.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION.0=Off
value.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION.1=On
option.LENS_DROPS=Lens drops
option.LENS_DROPS.comment=Out in the rain, drops land on the picture, show the landscape upside down in them, then dry; coming out of water, the picture streams for a few seconds.
value.LENS_DROPS.0=Off
value.LENS_DROPS.1=On
option.CONNECTED_GLASS=Connected glass
option.CONNECTED_GLASS.comment=Glass blocks and panes lose their frame where they touch other glass, so a glass wall reads as one pane.
value.CONNECTED_GLASS.0=Off
value.CONNECTED_GLASS.1=On
option.PIXEL_SHADOWS=Pixel shadows
option.PIXEL_SHADOWS.comment=Shadows on blocks follow the game's pixels: each texel takes the shadow of its centre, so shadow edges step pixel by pixel like the rest of the drawing.
value.PIXEL_SHADOWS.0=Off
value.PIXEL_SHADOWS.1=On
option.EAVES_DRIPS=Eaves drips
option.EAVES_DRIPS.comment=During and after rain, water drips from the edges of roofs, balconies and overhangs.
value.EAVES_DRIPS.0=Off
value.EAVES_DRIPS.1=On
option.LENS_SNOW=Snow on the lens
option.LENS_SNOW.comment=In snowfall, flakes land on the picture, melt and turn into drops.
value.LENS_SNOW.0=Off
value.LENS_SNOW.1=On
option.SOIL_STEAM=Steaming ground
option.SOIL_STEAM.comment=When the sun returns after a shower on warm soil, pale vapour rises from the ground and fades as it dries.
value.SOIL_STEAM.0=Off
value.SOIL_STEAM.1=On
option.PLANKTON=Glowing plankton
option.PLANKTON.comment=At night in warm seas, the foam of waves, wakes and falls lights up in a cold blue.
value.PLANKTON.0=Off
value.PLANKTON.1=On
option.PLANKTON_STRENGTH=Plankton glow
option.PLANKTON_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly the plankton glows.
option.DUST_DEVILS=Dust devils
option.DUST_DEVILS.comment=In deserts and dry savannas, in fine weather, columns of sand spin, wander and fall apart.
value.DUST_DEVILS.0=Off
value.DUST_DEVILS.1=On
option.MIRAGE=Mirages
option.MIRAGE.comment=In scorching deserts, far away, the ground reflects the sky in a shimmering sheet that looks like water.
value.MIRAGE.0=Off
value.MIRAGE.1=On
option.DIAMOND_DUST=Diamond dust
option.DIAMOND_DUST.comment=In dry, clear, bitter cold, the sunlit air fills with tiny glittering ice crystals.
value.DIAMOND_DUST.0=Off
value.DIAMOND_DUST.1=On
option.SKY_MOONBOW=Moonbow
option.SKY_MOONBOW.comment=At night after rain, under a full or nearly full moon, a pale, almost white arc opposite the moon.
option.EARTHSHINE=Earthshine
option.EARTHSHINE.comment=The dark part of the moon is faintly visible in bluish grey, lit by the Earth, more so when the moon is a thin crescent. Works with any moon texture that keeps the vanilla layout of phases.
option.MOON_UPRIGHT=Upright moon
option.MOON_UPRIGHT.comment=The moon keeps its straight edges, as the game shows it, instead of leaning with the tilted path of the sun and moon.
value.SKY_MOONBOW.0=Off
value.SKY_MOONBOW.1=On
option.SKY_NOCTILUCENT=Noctilucent clouds
option.SKY_NOCTILUCENT.comment=Some evenings and mornings, long after sunset, a veil of electric blue ripples glows low on the horizon on the sun's side.
value.SKY_NOCTILUCENT.0=Off
value.SKY_NOCTILUCENT.1=On
option.SUN_PILLAR=Sun pillar
option.SUN_PILLAR.comment=In clear, bitter cold, at sunrise and sunset, a column of light rises above the sun.
value.SUN_PILLAR.0=Off
value.SUN_PILLAR.1=On
option.SHORE_SPRAY=Shore spray
option.SHORE_SPRAY.comment=In strong wind, water beating the shores throws white puffs of spray that the wind carries off.
value.SHORE_SPRAY.0=Off
value.SHORE_SPRAY.1=On
option.SPRAY_RAINBOW=Rainbow in the spray
